{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1545","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1545","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1545\",\"parent_revision\":\"bd82403fc708f2d544b8699c6c7a6941dff916cf36d5d66c3edc17caa00ba900\",\"root_revision\":\"bd82403fc708f2d544b8699c6c7a6941dff916cf36d5d66c3edc17caa00ba900\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nlive_validation_step.py returns DEFERRED_SKILL for claude-skill sentinel without calling run_live_validation_skill.py. T5 corrected the false doc claim. This item evaluates Option A (wire the actual call in live_validation_step.py) vs Option B (confirm manual-invocation intent) and implements the chosen resolution so docs and code agree definitively.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `live_validation_step.py` returns `DEFERRED_SKILL` for the `claude-skill` sentinel without calling `run_live_validation_skill.py` \u2014 Evidence: `live_validation_step.py:97-98` \u2014 `if live_val == SENTINEL_CLAUDE_SKILL: return LiveValidationOutcome(result=LiveValidationResult.DEFERRED_SKILL, command=live_val)` \u2014 no call to `run_live_validation_skill` anywhere in the file\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `run_live_validation_skill.py` is a standalone script with its own `main()` and CLI interface \u2014 Evidence: `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_live_validation_skill.py:40-65` \u2014 designed for command-line invocation (`argparse`, `sys.exit`), not for import/call from another Python module\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `run_live_validation_skill.py` calls into `plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/run_eval.py` via `run_single_query()` \u2014 Evidence: `run_live_validation_skill.py:18-23` \u2014 resolves path to skill-creator scripts and imports `run_single_query`\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** `run_live_validation_skill.py` requires `--skill-path` and `--query` arguments \u2014 Evidence: `run_live_validation_skill.py:43-48` \u2014 both are `required=True` argparse arguments; `check_live_validation()` has neither and could not supply them without additional manifest fields\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** Test `test_claude_skill_sentinel_deferred_no_gap` passes and documents DEFERRED_SKILL as the correct result \u2014 Evidence: `test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py:174-183`\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** The python3 and python3-cli language manifests declare `live_validation: 'claude-skill'` \u2014 Evidence: `test_feature_verifier_live_validation.py:187-213` \u2014 two tests assert this against the real manifest files\\n\\n**[VERIFIED]** No docstring or comment in `live_validation_step.py` claims `run_live_validation_skill.py` is called automatically \u2014 Evidence: `live_validation_step.py:63-76` (docstring) \u2014 the docstring says `claude-skill \u2192 DEFERRED_SKILL (no gap)`, consistent with manual-invocation intent\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nType: **missing-guardrail** (documentation gap, not a code defect)\\n\\nThe code behaviour is internally consistent: `DEFERRED_SKILL` signals that live validation is delegated to a separate invocation. The gap is that no documentation explicitly records this as intentional design, leaving future maintainers uncertain whether the wiring is missing or deliberate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/live_validation_step.py:63-76` \u2014 docstring update (add manual-invocation note)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/live_validation_step.py:97-98` \u2014 add inline comment confirming intentional design\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/run_live_validation_skill.py` \u2014 read-only reference; no changes\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nSeverity: **Low** (documentation gap only)\\n\\n- Future maintainers may incorrectly treat the missing call as a bug and attempt to wire Option A, potentially breaking the Step 8 protocol contract.\\n- No runtime failure occurs; behaviour is correct today.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFollow-up to **P1526** (live-validation-manifest-v2). Independent of #1544 \u2014 both are P1526 quality-gate follow-ups; can be worked in parallel. This issue must be resolved before any future work proposes Option A wiring, to prevent scope creep.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nEstimate: **XS**\\nReasoning: Two comment/docstring edits in one file, no logic changes, no new tests required. The decision has been made above; implementation is mechanical.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:89d14439b74844febd34e81275163cb0 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNot applicable \u2014 this is not a runtime defect. The `DEFERRED_SKILL` return path is tested and correct. The issue is the absence of explicit documentation that this is intentional.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **reconcile claude-skill sentinel wiring between docs and implementation** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Quality gate follow-up from P1526 (live-validation-manifest-v2) \u2014 code-reviewer T1 and doc-drift-auditor T4\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| task-plan | /home/ubuntulinuxqa2/.dh/projects/-home-ubuntulinuxqa2-repos-claude_skills/plan/P1529-live-validation-manifest-v2-followup-2.yaml | current |  | 2026-04-05T05:49:08Z |\\n\\n---\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Decision\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Option A \u2014 Wire the actual call in `live_validation_step.py`\\n\\nCall `run_live_validation_skill.py` (via subprocess or direct import) from within `check_live_validation()` when sentinel is `claude-skill`.\\n\\n**Pros:**\\n- Automated end-to-end: feature-verifier invokes the skill check without manual steps\\n\\n**Cons:**\\n- `run_live_validation_skill.py` requires `--skill-path` and `--query` \u2014 neither is available from the language manifest or `project_root` alone; `check_live_validation()` has no way to supply them without additional manifest schema fields\\n- Would conflate two distinct concerns: live validation outcome reporting (Step 8) and skill activation evaluation (a separate eval workflow)\\n- `run_single_query` calls `claude -p`, making `check_live_validation()` a long-running, Claude-dependent operation \u2014 inconsistent with the lightweight subprocess model used for all other sentinel values\\n- Would require manifest schema extension to carry `skill_path` and `query` \u2014 scope expansion beyond P1526\\n\\n**Verdict:** Not feasible without significant manifest schema changes and a design decision about embedding eval queries in manifests.\\n\\n### Option B \u2014 Confirm manual-invocation intent and document it\\n\\nKeep `DEFERRED_SKILL` as-is. Add a code comment in `live_validation_step.py` and a docstring note explaining that `claude-skill` defers to manual invocation of `run_live_validation_skill.py`. Update the feature-verifier agent's Step 8 documentation to state this explicitly.\\n\\n**Pros:**\\n- No code change required; existing tests already assert the correct behaviour\\n- Matches the actual design: the feature-verifier reports DEFERRED_SKILL and the caller decides whether/when to invoke the skill evaluator\\n- `run_live_validation_skill.py` is a CLI tool by design (shebang, argparse, sys.exit) \u2014 its contract is invocation, not import\\n\\n**Cons:**\\n- Requires a documentation edit to make intent explicit\\n\\n**Verdict:** Correct resolution. The behaviour is by design; the gap is documentation only.\\n\\n### Recommendation: **Option B**\\n\\nEvidence: `run_live_validation_skill.py` is architecturally a CLI tool, not a library function. It cannot be called from `check_live_validation()` without `--skill-path` and `--query` that are unavailable at that call site. The docstring already states `DEFERRED_SKILL (no gap)`. Option A would require manifest schema changes scoped beyond this issue. Option B closes the documentation gap with zero risk.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria Groomed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] A code comment is added above `live_validation_step.py:97-98` (the `SENTINEL_CLAUDE_SKILL` branch) explaining that `DEFERRED_SKILL` is intentional \u2014 the caller is responsible for invoking `run_live_validation_skill.py` with the appropriate `--skill-path` and `--query` arguments\\n- [ ] The `check_live_validation()` docstring (lines 63-76) is updated to include a note: `claude-skill` defers to manual invocation of `run_live_validation_skill.py --skill-path <path> --query <prompt>`\\n- [ ] No change is made to the `DEFERRED_SKILL` return value or `LiveValidationResult` enum\\n- [ ] No change is made to `run_live_validation_skill.py`\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/scripts/live_validation_step.py` exits 0\\n- [ ] Existing test `test_claude_skill_sentinel_deferred_no_gap` continues to pass unchanged\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"852e1a99c3af8b1b86b02294b014bdb6950fffdfc70b846ab963b57877b3fc0a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCQL2A\"}"}